{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1370,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of us hear the word \"evolution\" and think\nof the process by which species change and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5500,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adapt and maybe turn into other species or\ngo extinct - but that's specifically the evolution"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of life forms by means of natural selection.\nThe word \"evolution\" in general just means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14160,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"change or development\", and there are plenty\nof other things that can evolve, or change,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18270,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in plenty of other ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19790,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the universe can evolve, that\nis, change, according to the laws of physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23700,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- galaxies form, planets and moons orbit,\nstars explode, etc. This doesn't mean there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28250,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any sort of cosmic \"survival of the fittest\"\ngoing on - that would be natural selection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32570,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not evolution. Similarly, the demographic\nmakeup of the United States can evolve as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36600,
    "dDurationMs": 3959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "children are born, young people move to cities,\nimmigrants arrive in the country, etc. In"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40559,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this sense, evolution just means change, and\nno one can deny that these these changes are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44199,
    "dDurationMs": 2101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happening - the evidence is overwhelming!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46300,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, around the time Charles Darwin\nwas doing his research, scientists (including"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50769,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Darwin himself) had begun amassing piles - literally\n- of evidence that showed that the nature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53999,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of life on earth had changed quite significantly\nover time: our oldest rocks show no signs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58839,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of life, while newer and newer rocks reveal\nfossilized plankton, seaweed, snails, fish,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63629,
    "dDurationMs": 5391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trees, insects, dinosaurs, mammals, and so\non. There absolutely was and is no denying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69020,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fact that life on earth changes - and\nchange over time is what \"evolution\" means."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74160,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What Darwin proposed with his theory of natural\nselection was an explanation for HOW this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78340,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "change (which is stupidly well supported by\nevidence) could have occurred naturally."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81460,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of it like the Challenger disaster\nof 1986: all the evidence showed that the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86240,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collection of molecules named \"Challenger\"\nhad tragically changed/evolved from a space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89790,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shuttle and its rocket boosters into a cloud\nof gas and debris shortly after launch (though"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93830,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we normally call this kind of evolution \"exploding\").\nThe question for scientists at the time was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95860,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to understand and explain HOW the explosion\nhad happened so they could prevent it in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99230,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future. Ultimately, it was the Theory of Frozen\nO-rings in the Rocket Boosters, popularized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103990,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Richard Feynman, that provided a satisfactory\nexplanation for the cause of the disaster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108110,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you're welcome to disagree with Feynman's\nexplanation for the explosion, or Darwin's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112020,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explanation for how life on earth changes,\nbut they're pretty darn good explanations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115540,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for these incredibly well documented examples\nof change in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118920,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the end, the universe will go on evolving\nregardless of whether you and I believe in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123030,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it or understand it, and perhaps the best\nthing to do is to remember that it's ok for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127110,
    "dDurationMs": 3579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our beliefs and opinions and understandings\nto evolve, too. That's part of life, and it's"
    } ]
  } ]
}
